00:34.050 --> 00:37.050
Anyway, this exercise is another one

00:37.050 --> 00:39.480
that is asking you to clone,

00:39.480 --> 00:42.900
to download an existing starter repository.

00:42.900 --> 00:45.990
So I still realize we have not really covered clone.

00:45.990 --> 00:49.320
You've cloned at least one time in a prior exercise.

00:49.320 --> 00:51.510
This is another example where I'm just gonna ask you

00:51.510 --> 00:52.680
to run this command.

00:52.680 --> 00:55.200
And just trust me, it gives you a repository

00:55.200 --> 00:56.310
I've made for you.

00:56.310 --> 00:59.820
We are on the verge, the cusp of learning about git clone,

00:59.820 --> 01:02.220
but for now, just run this at the beginning.

01:02.220 --> 01:04.020
So as always, this link is available

01:04.020 --> 01:05.730
as a resource with this video.

01:05.730 --> 01:07.410
I highly recommend you do the exercise.

01:07.410 --> 01:08.880
I think it's kind of a fun one.

01:08.880 --> 01:12.570
It's based on the lyrics to the Beatles song, "Yesterday,"

01:12.570 --> 01:16.470
which originally Paul McCartney wrote the melody

01:16.470 --> 01:19.560
and he sang it in his head and to friends

01:19.560 --> 01:21.120
using scrambled eggs.

01:21.120 --> 01:24.630
And then there's a whole bunch of lyrics he actually wrote

01:24.630 --> 01:26.220
that are all based around scrambled eggs.

01:26.220 --> 01:28.920
So the history of this repository, actually,

01:28.920 --> 01:32.910
includes my fictionalized evolution of those lyrics.

01:32.910 --> 01:34.710
So you'll see if you clone this repository,

01:34.710 --> 01:35.670
we'll start there.

01:35.670 --> 01:38.130
Make sure that we're not in a git repository

01:38.130 --> 01:39.330
when we do this.

01:39.330 --> 01:42.360
And then just paste that line. Okay?

01:42.360 --> 01:46.140
That now makes us a folder called "yesterday-exercise."

01:46.140 --> 01:49.860
So if we "cd" into that, the next step is to,

01:49.860 --> 01:52.260
well we should see a file called "lyrics," okay?

01:52.260 --> 01:54.780
And then we take a look at the commit history.

01:54.780 --> 01:57.030
So I'll just do that with you right now.

01:57.030 --> 01:58.317
Lemme do "oneline."

01:59.940 --> 02:02.580
You can see that there are eight different commits

02:02.580 --> 02:05.580
that you have already just by cloning.

02:05.580 --> 02:08.310
So this first kind of batch here

02:08.310 --> 02:11.070
all have to do with "Scrambled Egg" lyrics.

02:11.070 --> 02:12.660
So I wrote, I copied and pasted,

02:12.660 --> 02:14.820
but the original first verse, second verse,

02:14.820 --> 02:16.590
the chorus, then I finished it.

02:16.590 --> 02:19.297
And then this is the rework where it became

02:19.297 --> 02:21.060
"Yesterday" instead of "Scrambled Eggs"

02:21.060 --> 02:23.130
broken into four different commits.

02:23.130 --> 02:27.510
Okay, so your task is, well there's a bunch of tasks.

02:27.510 --> 02:29.010
Is to follow the instructions.

02:29.010 --> 02:31.680
I won't just walk through them all right now before I do it.

02:31.680 --> 02:33.990
But basically at one point I ask you to go back

02:33.990 --> 02:35.160
and check out a commit.

02:35.160 --> 02:37.080
You'll go into detached HEAD.

02:37.080 --> 02:39.330
And then I ask you to go back, leave detached HEAD

02:39.330 --> 02:40.980
and go back to the master branch.

02:40.980 --> 02:43.380
Then I ask you to go find a particular commit

02:43.380 --> 02:45.540
where I finish the original lyrics,

02:45.540 --> 02:48.600
and then create a branch based upon that commit.

02:48.600 --> 02:51.510
So that we'll have one branch called "scrambled-eggs"

02:51.510 --> 02:52.890
that actually has all the lyrics

02:52.890 --> 02:56.550
from that original version called "Scrambled Eggs."

02:56.550 --> 02:59.580
And then I'm gonna ask you to make a serious change,

02:59.580 --> 03:02.880
delete everything in the "lyrics.txt" file,

03:02.880 --> 03:04.260
and then save that file.

03:04.260 --> 03:06.300
But don't add and commit, just save.

03:06.300 --> 03:08.370
And then using a git command,

03:08.370 --> 03:13.080
so not using Command Z or undo, but using a git command,

03:13.080 --> 03:14.880
discard those changes you made

03:14.880 --> 03:18.210
so that you end up with the lyrics back in the file.

03:18.210 --> 03:21.960
Then we move on to something slightly humorous

03:21.960 --> 03:24.810
where I found some parody lyrics from this website.

03:24.810 --> 03:26.260
I did not write these myself.

03:27.240 --> 03:32.220
And these parody lyrics have to do with 404 pages.

03:32.220 --> 03:36.390
So lyrics set to "Yesterday," but about 404 pages.

03:36.390 --> 03:38.760
So I just ask you to copy some of them,

03:38.760 --> 03:40.980
paste it into the "lyrics" file.

03:40.980 --> 03:42.810
and add and commit on the master branch.

03:42.810 --> 03:43.800
And then do it again.

03:43.800 --> 03:47.430
Finish the song out, add and commit on the master branch.

03:47.430 --> 03:48.870
After more consideration, you realize

03:48.870 --> 03:50.340
you don't actually want those two commits

03:50.340 --> 03:51.420
on the master branch.

03:51.420 --> 03:53.910
So I would like for you to move them.

03:53.910 --> 03:57.270
And the way that we'll do that is by undoing them.

03:57.270 --> 03:59.190
So we're going to remove those two commits

03:59.190 --> 04:00.023
from the master branch.

04:00.023 --> 04:01.410
We've seen a command to do that.

04:01.410 --> 04:04.260
However, I don't want you to lose those changes.

04:04.260 --> 04:07.290
I want you to keep the changes in your working directory.

04:07.290 --> 04:11.220
So you may need to rewatch a video to learn how to do that.

04:11.220 --> 04:13.350
Keep the changes, undo the two commits.

04:13.350 --> 04:15.930
Then you can create a new branch called "404,"

04:15.930 --> 04:18.090
switch over to it, and then

04:18.090 --> 04:19.410
those changes will come with you.

04:19.410 --> 04:21.480
You can add and commit them on the 404 branch

04:21.480 --> 04:23.340
and go back to the master branch

04:23.340 --> 04:25.500
and we'll have the original lyrics.

04:25.500 --> 04:28.320
So don't just, you know, listen to me.

04:28.320 --> 04:31.290
Read the the exercise, read the bullet points.

04:31.290 --> 04:33.240
I think it's pretty step-by-step.

04:33.240 --> 04:36.330
You'll need to use most of the commands we talked about

04:36.330 --> 04:39.210
and you may need to reference either the git docs

04:39.210 --> 04:41.520
or the earlier videos in this section.

04:41.520 --> 04:42.960
So I'm gonna go ahead and do it.

04:42.960 --> 04:45.092
I really recommend you do it.

04:45.092 --> 04:46.620
You know, it kind of takes me forever to make these things.

04:46.620 --> 04:49.050
So I hope you get something out of them.

04:49.050 --> 04:50.370
Anyway, here we go.

04:50.370 --> 04:51.420
So I already cloned.

04:51.420 --> 04:53.850
We already saw that there was eight commits in there.

04:53.850 --> 04:56.490
I'm going to check out the very first commit.

04:56.490 --> 05:00.570
And first, I'm just gonna open up the "lyrics" file, right?

05:00.570 --> 05:03.573
There's one file, so I'll just open it up in VS code.

05:04.800 --> 05:06.750
And I'll do this side-by-side.

05:06.750 --> 05:08.520
Okay, so there is the lyrics,

05:08.520 --> 05:11.070
the complete lyrics for, "Yesterday,"

05:11.070 --> 05:13.980
although actually I did leave off the final verse.

05:13.980 --> 05:18.060
Anyway, what we're going to do now is go back to the commit.

05:18.060 --> 05:20.340
That was the very, very first commit.

05:20.340 --> 05:22.950
So "git log," just do "oneline,"

05:22.950 --> 05:26.283
and I'm gonna copy this hash, and then check it out.

05:27.187 --> 05:29.040
"Git checkout" that hash.

05:29.040 --> 05:30.930
And this is the very first commit.

05:30.930 --> 05:32.760
We are going to immediately leave.

05:32.760 --> 05:34.410
We saw those lyrics, right?

05:34.410 --> 05:37.380
Those are different than what was just in that file.

05:37.380 --> 05:38.940
We're gonna go back to the master branch.

05:38.940 --> 05:41.010
So I can just do a "git switch" master,

05:41.010 --> 05:45.480
or just "git switch -" to go back to where I was.

05:45.480 --> 05:48.660
And now we see "Yesterday," the actual lyrics.

05:48.660 --> 05:50.490
Next, go back to the commit

05:50.490 --> 05:52.290
where the original version of the lyrics

05:52.290 --> 05:53.790
was first completed.

05:53.790 --> 05:57.360
This commit has the message "finish original lyrics,"

05:57.360 --> 05:59.340
and then create a branch called "scrambled-eggs"

05:59.340 --> 06:01.410
based on that commit.

06:01.410 --> 06:02.967
So we'll do a "git log."

06:03.967 --> 06:05.640
"Oneline."

06:05.640 --> 06:09.090
Let's find, there it is: "finish original lyrics,"

06:09.090 --> 06:10.830
copy that hash.

06:10.830 --> 06:12.000
We're going to check it out.

06:12.000 --> 06:14.640
This will be a detached HEAD, which is okay.

06:14.640 --> 06:17.910
So here's the full "Scrambled Eggs" lyrics.

06:17.910 --> 06:20.640
So we're going to make a branch based upon this.

06:20.640 --> 06:21.780
I'm gonna switch to it.

06:21.780 --> 06:22.653
Let me clear.

06:23.803 --> 06:27.090
"-c," and it's called "scrambled-eggs."

06:27.090 --> 06:29.730
So now we're no longer in detached HEAD.

06:29.730 --> 06:32.790
We have these changes, from the earlier commit,

06:32.790 --> 06:34.713
but I can also switch back to master.

06:35.760 --> 06:37.620
And we don't have those changes here.

06:37.620 --> 06:38.940
I mean we do in the history,

06:38.940 --> 06:41.970
but currently in the working directory, we don't.

06:41.970 --> 06:44.010
Now, delete everything in the "lyrics" file

06:44.010 --> 06:46.950
on the master branch, and save.

06:46.950 --> 06:48.690
Uh oh, I didn't mean to do that.

06:48.690 --> 06:51.030
And ignoring the fact that I can just do command Z

06:51.030 --> 06:55.050
and undo it, using a git command, discard those changes.

06:55.050 --> 06:57.030
Okay, how do I do that?

06:57.030 --> 06:58.830
Well, there's a couple of options.

06:58.830 --> 07:01.200
The newer way of doing it is "git restore,"

07:01.200 --> 07:02.550
and then a file name.

07:02.550 --> 07:06.420
So "git restore lyrics," and there we are.

07:06.420 --> 07:09.720
But I can also recreate that.

07:09.720 --> 07:10.980
So I just saved again.

07:10.980 --> 07:13.140
I can do the older version.

07:13.140 --> 07:14.047
Whoopsies.

07:14.047 --> 07:18.357
"Git checkout HEAD," and then the file "lyrics."

07:19.380 --> 07:22.050
And there we go. Same thing. Okay?

07:22.050 --> 07:23.730
Next up I get a creative itch.

07:23.730 --> 07:25.050
