08:25.830 --> 08:28.590
So this is 404, this is 404.

08:28.590 --> 08:30.930
This is what I want to go back to.

08:30.930 --> 08:32.370
So two commits ago.

08:32.370 --> 08:34.170
Copy that hash.

08:34.170 --> 08:36.090
And then I'm gonna do a "git reset."

08:36.090 --> 08:38.700
But I'm not gonna do hard if you recall,

08:38.700 --> 08:42.990
which also updates the files and undoes the changes.

08:42.990 --> 08:44.700
It doesn't just delete the commits,

08:44.700 --> 08:46.170
it actually undoes changes.

08:46.170 --> 08:47.820
I'm not going to do that.

08:47.820 --> 08:50.550
As this document makes, I hope clear,

08:50.550 --> 08:52.260
keep the changes in your working directory.

08:52.260 --> 08:55.650
Just undo the two commits. Okay?

08:55.650 --> 08:57.810
So we don't see anything change over here,

08:57.810 --> 09:02.810
but if I do a "git log," we don't see those 404 commits.

09:03.750 --> 09:07.980
So now, I can make my new branch called "404."

09:07.980 --> 09:12.060
